      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;two-poems-john-astin&#34;&gt;Two Poems John Astin&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/discourses/teachers/enough_astin.htm&#34;&gt;TW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Author: John Astin&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure class=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/John-Astin_cover.gif&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/John-Astin_cover.gif&#34; alt=&#34;book cover&#34; title=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The following two poems are extracted from the book by John Astin: &lt;strong&gt;This Is Always Enough&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.integrativearts.com/&#34;&gt;John&amp;rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Buy John&amp;rsquo;s book from &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0955399955/fromtheunreat-20&#34;&gt;US&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0955399955/thespiritupat-21&#34;&gt;UK&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;See Book recommendation for &amp;lsquo;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/reading/read_neo.htm#astin&#34;&gt;This Is Always Enough&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Everything is&lt;br&gt;&#xA;welcomed here.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;The innkeeper&lt;br&gt;&#xA;refuses no visitors&lt;br&gt;&#xA;but beckons&lt;br&gt;&#xA;all to enter -&lt;br&gt;&#xA;every thought,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;every sensation,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;everything&lt;br&gt;&#xA;that appears&lt;br&gt;&#xA;and then disappears&lt;br&gt;&#xA;all are invited&lt;br&gt;&#xA;to the dance,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;this endless play&lt;br&gt;&#xA;of emptiness&lt;br&gt;&#xA;loving form,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;and wave&lt;br&gt;&#xA;loving sea.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
